nce used, preserve exact text in the context receipt |\n| UI preview/automatic synopsis | Display convenience | Local projection/cache | Usually regenerate |\n| Durable knowledge extracted from a Chat | Curated reusable knowledge | Knowledge Space Git repo | Only after explicit promotion |\n\nThe existing compaction summary is not a KB note. It is a versioned execution checkpoint with an exact message boundary; original messages remain canonical and unchanged. That is already the contract in [SPEC.md](/home/leon0399/.herdr/worktrees/llame/agentic-federation-and-distribution-direction/SPEC.md:35).\n\nLikewise, the proposed fork summaries are branch-specific derived artifacts. If a model actually receives one, the exact injected text matters for provenance and belongs in that Run’s context receipt. The research note already says this at [the concurrent-Chat reconciliation section](/home/leon0399/.herdr/worktrees/llame/agentic-federation-and-distribution-direction/docs/research/product-vision/2026-08-21-local-nodes-workspaces-and-distributed-execution.md:407).\n\n### Where Chats should live\n\nMy recommendation:\n\n```text\nCLI/daemon local DB ─┐\nAndroid local DB ────┼── portable llame sync protocol ── Hub Postgres + RLS\nDesktop local DB ────┘\n\nKnowledge repo ─────────────── Git protocol ───────────── Git remote\n```\n\n- **Hub:** keep Postgres. High confidence.\n- **Personal node:** probably SQLite or another embedded transactional store. Moderate confidence; do not lock the engine yet.\n- **Synchronization:** application-level and automatic—not PostgreSQL physical/logical replication, and not something the user manually performs.\n\nA local transaction would conceptually:\n\n1. Write the Chat/message/Run record.\n2. Append a sync envelope to an outbox in the same transaction.\n3. Upload unacknowledged envelopes when connected.\n4. Have the receiving node authenticate, validate, and apply them idempotently.\n5. Download accepted envelopes after a resumable cursor.