l replication, not quorum durability.\n\nOne important rule: anything displayed to the user should be locally journaled before display, but it need not be synchronized upstream first. Otherwise offline operation becomes dependent on remote availability.\n\nThe existing `run_events` implementation can remain the hosted llame executor’s recovery journal. It must not become the federation protocol; that would permanently couple every node to llame’s current worker and streaming internals.\n\nConfidence:\n\n- Three-layer separation: high.\n- Semantic checkpoint model: high.\n- Exact assistant-content checkpoint granularity: moderate; avoid choosing time/byte thresholds until measured.\n\nMy recommendation is to accept this contract, including the uncomfortable consequence that catastrophic node loss may discard the last incomplete, unsynchronized assistant block. Do you agree, or do you require every user-visible partial block to become portable immediately?\n\nThe older memory entry was discovery-only; this thread’s decisions supersede it.\n\n<oai-mem-citation>\n<citation_entries>\nMEMORY.md:1-10|note=[Used to distinguish the original discovery-only exploration from current approved decisions]\n</citation_entries>\n<rollout_ids>\n01a024bb-35e2-78a0-ba6f-97026dfea5ec\n</rollout_ids>\n</oai-mem-citation>",
